Summary: Store the PEB at %gs:0x60, where Windows code expects it
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 25.1.1
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c, dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c, dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
  Changes: verbatim
  Note: unmarked hunks (no CW HACK number) that go with CrossOver's
    D3DMetal support; CrossOver 26.3.0 still has them. Sikarugir 10.0_8
    ships it: ntdll.so writes %gs:0x60 in call_init_thunk (movq
    %rax,%gs:0x60 right after the %gs:0x30 and %gs:0x58 writes) and zeroes
    it before pthread_exit; the localtime hook's movabsq
    $0xcccc0000000225ff (jmp *2(%rip); int3; int3) is present
Upstream: differently (3a16aabb, Wine 10.5: GSBASE points at the TEB while
 PE code runs, through _thread_set_tsd_base)
Needed until: 10.5 (WineHQ 3a16aabb)
Why: 64-bit Windows code reads the PEB from %gs:0x60 (TEB->Peb), often
 inlined (NtCurrentPeb()). In Wine 10.0 on macOS %gs is the pthread TSD,
 not the TEB, and slot 0x60 belongs to libc's localtime(), so such code
 reads the wrong thing. Store the PEB there in every thread, hook
 localtime() to a thread-local localtime_r() so libc no longer uses the
 slot, and clear the slot before pthread_exit so libpthread's key
 destructor doesn't free() it. Measured on a 10.0 build (macOS 26.7.2):
 %gs:0x60 is the PEB in the main thread and a new thread.
Programs: none known; any 64-bit program or DLL that reads the PEB through
 %gs (CrossOver ties it to D3DMetal)
Risk: patches libsystem_c's localtime() in memory at start-up (a jump
 written into its code, the page made writable with mprotect), in every
 64-bit Wine process on 10.0
Uncertain: whether D3DMetal needs it (CrossOver's grouping, not verified).
 The localtime() hook works under Rosetta; not tried on an Intel Mac,
 where it depends on mprotect granting write access to the shared cache
 page (its result isn't checked).
Related: ntdll-preallocate-tls-expansion; the same cause (10.0's %gs is
 the pthread TSD), another TEB field

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index 2c4e1f4..9442a15 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1941,6 +1941,48 @@ static ULONG_PTR get_image_address(void)
     return 0;
 }
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__x86_64__)
+static __thread struct tm localtime_tls;
+struct tm *my_localtime(const time_t *timep)
+{
+    return localtime_r(timep, &localtime_tls);
+}
+
+static void hook(void *to_hook, const void *replace)
+{
+    size_t offset;
+
+    struct hooked_function
+    {
+        char jmp[8];
+        const void *dst;
+    } *hooked_function = to_hook;
+    ULONG_PTR intval = (UINT_PTR)to_hook;
+
+    intval -= (intval % 4096);
+    mprotect((void *)intval, 0x2000, PROT_EXEC | PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE);
+
+    /* The offset is from the end of the jmp instruction (6 bytes) to the start of the destination. */
+    offset = offsetof(struct hooked_function, dst) - offsetof(struct hooked_function, jmp) - 0x6;
+
+    /* jmp *(rip + offset) */
+    hooked_function->jmp[0] = 0xff;
+    hooked_function->jmp[1] = 0x25;
+    hooked_function->jmp[2] = offset;
+    hooked_function->jmp[3] = 0x00;
+    hooked_function->jmp[4] = 0x00;
+    hooked_function->jmp[5] = 0x00;
+    /* Filler */
+    hooked_function->jmp[6] = 0xcc;
+    hooked_function->jmp[7] = 0xcc;
+    /* Dest address absolute */
+    hooked_function->dst = replace;
+
+    //size = sizeof(*hooked_function);
+    //NtProtectVirtualMemory(proc, (void **)hooked_function, &size, old_protect, &old_protect);
+}
+#endif
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           start_main_thread
  */
@@ -1966,6 +2008,13 @@ static void start_main_thread(void)
     load_ntdll();
     load_wow64_ntdll( main_image_info.Machine );
     load_apiset_dll();
+
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__x86_64__)
+    /* This is necessary because we poke PEB into pthread TLS at offset 0x60. It is normally in use by
+     * localtime(), which is called a lot by system libraries. Make localtime() go away. */
+    hook(localtime, my_localtime);
+#endif
+
     server_init_process_done();
 }
 
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
